# SPDX-License-Identifier: MPL-2.0
import lib/cadkernel/brep_mesh.dl
import lib/cadkernel/brep_make.dl

function check mesh mass {boolean:passed} named {C string:label}:
    execute:
        if passed = false:
            print label as a line
            @intrinsic("call", "libc", "exit", nothing, 1)

function check mesh mass {a 64 bit floating-point number:value} near {a 64 bit floating-point number:expected} within {a 64 bit floating-point number:tolerance} named {C string:label}:
    execute:
        check mesh mass ((the absolute value of (value - expected)) <= tolerance) named label

set origins to a list containing (the cad zero vector3)
append (a cad vector3 with x 1000000000.0, y -2000000000.0 and z 3000000000.0) to origins
loop originIndex from 0 to the length of origins:
    set origin to the item at originIndex in origins
    set made to the cad cuboid at origin with size (a cad vector3 with x 2.0, y 3.0 and z 4.0)
    check mesh mass made's valid named "cuboid"
    set meshValue to the cad mesh of made's value with maximum angle (the cad default sampling angle) within 1e-9
    loop orientationIndex from 0 to 2:
        set properties to the cad inertial properties of meshValue
        check mesh mass properties's valid named "properties"
        check mesh mass properties's value's volume near 24.0 within 1e-9 named "volume"
        check mesh mass properties's value's centroid's x near (origin's x + 1.0) within 1e-6 named "centroid x"
        check mesh mass properties's value's centroid's y near (origin's y + 1.5) within 1e-6 named "centroid y"
        check mesh mass properties's value's centroid's z near (origin's z + 2.0) within 1e-6 named "centroid z"
        check mesh mass properties's value's principalMoments's x near 26.0 within 1e-8 named "principal x"
        check mesh mass properties's value's principalMoments's y near 40.0 within 1e-8 named "principal y"
        check mesh mass properties's value's principalMoments's z near 50.0 within 1e-8 named "principal z"
        loop triangleIndex from 0 to the length of meshValue's triangles:
            set triangleValue to the item at triangleIndex in meshValue's triangles
            set saved to triangleValue's second
            set triangleValue's second to triangleValue's third
            set triangleValue's third to saved
            replace item at index triangleIndex in meshValue's triangles with triangleValue
    free cad mesh meshValue
free origins

set emptyMesh to the cad mesh of (an empty cad body) with maximum angle (the cad default sampling angle) within 1e-9
check mesh mass (((the cad inertial properties of emptyMesh)'s valid) = false) named "empty"
free cad mesh emptyMesh
print "cadkernel brep mesh mass: PASS" as a line
